 ],
 "literal": "Water-drying not knowing, rooted in the ground, / dark-clustered nocci's eye-pleasing bright foliage, / we saw as a garland on the delicate, wide waist of women wearing soft jewels; now indeed, / mingled with frightening blood, its form hidden, / that chipped garland, mistaking it for flesh, / we saw a kite take and soar with, / because of the way the valor-desiring warrior fought!",
 "translation": "We once saw the bright, eye-pleasing foliage of the dark-clustered nocci tree, which grows deep in the soil and never knows a lack of water, worn as a garland on the delicate, wide hips of women adorned with soft jewels. But now, because of the way the valor-loving warrior fought, we saw a kite seize that very garland—now chipped, stained with terrifying blood, and its true form hidden—and soar high into the sky, mistaking it for a piece of flesh.",
 "modern": "வேர்கள் எப்போதும் நீரற்றுப் போகாதவாறு நிலத்தோடு பொருந்திய, கரிய பூங்கொத்துகளைக் கொண்ட நொச்சியின் அழகிய பிரகாசமான தழைகளை, மென்மையான அணிகலன்களை அணிந்த பெண்களின் மெல்லிய பரந்த அல்குலில் மாலையாகக் கண்டோம். ஆனால் இப்போது, வீரம் மிக்க அந்த வீரன் போரிட்ட தன்மையால், அச்சம் தரும் குருதியோடு கலந்து தன் வடிவம் மறைந்து, சிதைந்துபோன அந்த நொச்சி மாலையை, ஊன் என்று தவறாக நினைத்துப் பருந்து ஒன்று கவ்விக்கொண்டு மேலே பறந்து செல்வதை நாம் கண்டோம்.",
 "explanation": "This poem belongs to the Nocci tiṇai, which traditionally depicts the defense of a fortress, and the theme is 'falling in battle' (ceruviṭai vīḻtal). The poet, Veṟi Pāṭiya Kāmaakkaṇṇiyār, contrasts the peaceful past of the nocci foliage with its tragic present on the battlefield. Formerly, the lush, green leaves of the nocci tree, which grows near water, were woven into beautiful garlands to adorn the hips of delicate women. Now, after a fierce battle, the brave warrior who wore the nocci garland as a defensive symbol lies dead. His garland is so drenched in blood and mutilated that a hovering kite mistakes it for raw flesh and flies away with it. This stark, gruesome image powerfully conveys the tragedy of war and the ultimate sacrifice of the young warrior.",
 "model": "gemini-3.5-flash",
